                            <comment id="15858044" author="drigor" created="Wed, 8 Feb 2017 14:25:35 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hello!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Could you please explain, why order is important?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15858063" author="prabhjyotsingh" created="Wed, 8 Feb 2017 14:38:06 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Yes, because this is always honoured as long as the name is same as default name. But if a user changes the default interpreter name, for example in the default configuration in which zeppelin is shipped is; &quot;spark&quot; is default interpreter, now if user decides to change this name to &quot;spark_2&quot; or say we decides to have two spark interpreter with different names, in both of these cases the one which does not have name &quot;spark&quot; comes to the last, and other becomes default.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;IMHO, this should behave like we do order by on a table. Hence, in this case first all spark interpreters together, then say all JDCB, angular and so on.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Screen shot for the same is available on this PR &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/1992&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/1992&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
